      "body": "## Background\n\nIssue #44278.  `calculate_metrics` in `python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py`\ncomputes `max_concurrent_requests` by building a per-second bucket\nhistogram — for each request it increments every integer-second bucket\nfrom request start through request end (inclusive), then takes `np.max`.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe bucket approach cannot recover actual overlap **within** a second.\nIssue reproduction: five sequential non-overlapping requests with lifetimes\n`[10.0000, 10.0625)`, `[10.1250, 10.1875)`, `[10.2500, 10.3125)`,\n`[10.3750, 10.4375)`, `[10.5000, 10.5625)` — all touch the first\none-second bucket, so the old code reports **peak=5**.  The true maximum\nsimultaneous count is **1**.\n\nThe same issue also double-counts boundary handoffs — `[10, 11)` followed\nby `[11, 12)` — because the range iterates `request_end_second + 1`.\n\n## Solution\n\nReplace the scalar peak with a **sweep line** over half-open `[start, end)`\nintervals:\n\n```python\nevents = [(start, +1), (end, -1) for each successful request]\nevents.sort()\nrunning = peak = 0\nfor _, delta in events:\n    running += delta\n    peak = max(peak, running)\n```\n\nThe per-second `concurrent_requests_per_second` array is **preserved**\nfor the existing `plot_throughput` output.  Only the scalar peak value\nchanges.\n\n## Verification\n\nAgainst the issue's reproduction example:\n\n```\n5 sequential non-overlapping requests — OLD peak=5, NEW peak=1 ✓\n2 truly overlapping requests           — OLD peak=2, NEW peak=2 ✓\nBoundary [0,1) + [1,2) half-open      — OLD peak=2, NEW peak=1 ✓\n```\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38609202462](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38609202462)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38609202674](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38609202674)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38609202454](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38609202454)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
